<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/talks-ted-semantic-execution> {
  ex:ted-semantic-pipeline a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Describe the pipeline, not one fixed tool"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:ted-semantic-pipeline-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-semantic-execution ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-semantic-pipeline-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "Apply the shared processing model to the TED workflow. Each task is specified as an atomic ProcessingStep, hence a ProcessingUnit, with named input, output and parameter ports. A composite ProcessingPipeline records the step instances, their run targets and explicit compatible output-to-input connections. Import converts Shimadzu GQD data to EICs; qPeaks produces features; joint fitting produces components; marker selection returns marker areas; external calibration produces polymer-content results. EIC contracts describe time, ion channels and intensities with their units; feature/component contracts preserve identities, fit/area information and shared-profile membership; marker results link selected areas to their components and polymer assignment. The diagram summarizes the main data path, not every required port. Window sizes, fitting rules and marker definitions are explicit configuration. External calibration additionally needs its calibration data/model and, for normalized content, sample-mass metadata and units. Implementations are bound separately. A replacement is possible only if it meets the same contract and scientific validation requirements; semantics does not make arbitrary tools interchangeable. This is a teaching-level description, not a newly deployed executable workflow."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-semantic-execution ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-event-execution a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "From a finished measurement to an automatic run"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:ted-event-execution-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-semantic-execution ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-event-execution-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "The engine and described pipelines already exist, according to the speaker; the complete automation system remains under development and is not yet available. A pipeline is the schema of steps and connections followed by the engine, not a processing service beside it. A completed measurement and fully saved, available file cause a ready event. Event handling starts execution according to the selected pipeline schema. The engine produces a completed report containing results and provenance. After the event handler registers report completion, it initiates storage of that report and its provenance in the data server. Measurement readiness and report completion are distinct event types: a measurement-ready event must not cause storage of an unfinished report. File creation alone is insufficient. Permissions, duplicate events, retries, failure reporting and storage confirmation still require explicit integration; no exactly-once or deployed end-to-end guarantee is claimed. This is a proposed system architecture, not another data-processing pipeline or a substitute for scientific validation."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-semantic-execution ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-automatic-run-points a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Describe once, execute through bound steps, trigger on a ready measurement."@en ; cd:hasKeyPoint ex:ted-auto-p1, ex:ted-auto-p2, ex:ted-auto-p3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-auto-p1 a cd:KeyPoint ; cd:position 1 ; cd:body "**Already implemented:** engine and semantically described pipelines"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-auto-p2 a cd:KeyPoint ; cd:position 2 ; cd:body "**In development:** complete automation system, not yet available"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-auto-p3 a cd:KeyPoint ; cd:position 3 ; cd:body "==Completed reports are registered, then stored in the data server=="@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
}
<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/sources/talks-ted-semantic-execution> {
  ex:ted-source-semantic-execution a cd:Source ; dct:title "Speaker specification: semantic TED pipeline and event-driven execution" ; dct:creator "Gerrit Renner" ; dct:identifier "issue-294/semantic-pipeline-engine-events" ; dct:description "Author-supplied engine capability and event-triggered measurement-processing scenario. The architecture separates declarative workflows, execution and event handling. No deployment, readiness integration, performance benchmark or fault-tolerance guarantee is independently demonstrated by these slides."@en ; cd:supportsResource ex:ted-semantic-pipeline-definition, ex:ted-event-execution-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
}
<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/diagrams/talks-ted-semantic-execution> {
  ex:ted-semantic-pipeline-flow a cd:FlowDiagram ; skos:prefLabel "The TED workflow as specialized ProcessingSteps"@en ; cd:body "Each card is a ProcessingStep and therefore a ProcessingUnit. Explicit compatible port connections form a ProcessingPipeline; implementations are bound separately. Main data path shown; calibration data and sample metadata are additional requirements."@en ; cd:hasDiagramNode ex:ted-sem-import, ex:ted-sem-peaks, ex:ted-sem-components, ex:ted-sem-markers, ex:ted-sem-calibrate ; cd:hasDiagramEdge ex:ted-sem-connect1, ex:ted-sem-connect2, ex:ted-sem-connect3, ex:ted-sem-connect4 ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-semantic-execution ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-sem-import a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Import"@en ; cd:body "ProcessingStep\nIN: GQD files\nOUT: EICs"@en ; cd:visualMotif "data-import" ; cd:visualMotifRole "highlight" ; dct:references ex:ted-semantic-pipeline ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-sem-peaks a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Find peaks"@en ; cd:body "ProcessingStep\nIN: EICs\nOUT: features"@en ; cd:visualMotif "peak-search" ; cd:visualMotifRole "highlight" ; dct:references ex:ted-qpeaks ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-sem-components a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Form components"@en ; cd:body "ProcessingStep\nIN: features\nOUT: components"@en ; cd:visualMotif "shared-peak-shape" ; cd:visualMotifRole "highlight" ; dct:references ex:ted-peak-components ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-sem-markers a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 4 ; skos:prefLabel "Select markers"@en ; cd:body "ProcessingStep\nIN: components\nOUT: marker areas"@en ; cd:visualMotif "marker-selection" ; cd:visualMotifRole "highlight" ; dct:references ex:ted-polymer-markers ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-sem-calibrate a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 5 ; skos:prefLabel "Calibrate"@en ; cd:body "ProcessingStep\nIN: marker areas\nOUT: polymer content"@en ; cd:visualMotif "regression" ; cd:visualMotifRole "highlight" ; dct:references ex:ted-running-calibration ; cd:authoredResource true .
